.*
.* WRKJRNA: a journal's attributes, its receiver directory (F15) and
.* the objects it journals (F14). No golden: the pub400 account owns
.* no journal (title and keys).
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STAMPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 19'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=JRN CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ATTRCV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ATTRCVLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=ASP CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=JRNSTATE CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQ CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQLIB CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MNGRCV CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=DLTRCV CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJCOUNT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=RCV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=RCVLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=RCVSTS CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=RCVATT CLASS=STAMPCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=IMAGES CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OMTJRNE CLASS=NAMECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=RCVS VARS='OPT RCV RCVLIB RCVSTS RCVATT'.
:LISTDEF NAME=OBJS VARS='OBJ OBJLIB OBJTYPE IMAGES OMTJRNE'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/JAKEYS' NAME=JAKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F14 ACTION='RETURN 14'.F14=Display journaled objects
:KEYI KEY=F15 ACTION='RETURN 15'.F15=Work with receiver directory
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/SUBKEYS' NAME=SUBKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJRNA KEYL=JAKEYS HELP=WRKJRNA ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Journal Attributes
:DATA DEPTH='*'.
:DATACOL WIDTH=40.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRN' VAR=JRN USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ATTRCV' VAR=ATTRCV USAGE=OUTPUT.Attached receiver
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRNTEXT' VAR=JRNTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ASP' VAR=ASP USAGE=OUTPUT.ASP
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MSGQ' VAR=MSGQ USAGE=OUTPUT.Message queue
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MSGQLIB' VAR=MSGQLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/OBJCOUNT' VAR=OBJCOUNT USAGE=OUTPUT.Journaled objects
:DATACOL WIDTH=38.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRNLIB' VAR=JRNLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ATTRCVLIB' VAR=ATTRCVLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:DATAC.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRNSTATE' VAR=JRNSTATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal state
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MNGRCV' VAR=MNGRCV USAGE=OUTPUT.Manage receivers
:DATAI HELP='FLD/DLTRCV' VAR=DLTRCV USAGE=OUTPUT.Delete receivers
:EDATA.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJRNRD KEYL=SUBKEYS HELP=WRKJRNRD ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Receiver Directory
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRN' VAR=JRN USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal
:DATAIX VAR=JRNLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Library
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=RCVS.(No receivers)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRNRD/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?DLTJRNRCV JRNRCV(&RCVLIB./&RCV.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRNRD/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD DSPJRNRCVA JRNRCV(&RCVLIB./&RCV.)'.8=Display attributes
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKJRNRD/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RCV' VAR=RCV USAGE=OUTPUT.Receiver
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RCVLIB' VAR=RCVLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RCVSTS' VAR=RCVSTS USAGE=OUTPUT.Status
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RCVATT' VAR=RCVATT USAGE=OUTPUT.Attached
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPJRNOBJ KEYL=SUBKEYS HELP=DSPJRNOBJ ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Display Journaled Objects
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JRN' VAR=JRN USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal
:DATAIX VAR=JRNLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Library
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=OBJS.(No objects are journaled)
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJ' VAR=OBJ USAGE=OUTPUT.Object
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJLIB' VAR=OBJLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJTYPE' VAR=OBJTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/IMAGES' VAR=IMAGES USAGE=OUTPUT.Images
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OMTJRNE' VAR=OMTJRNE USAGE=OUTPUT.Omit
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRNA.Work with Journal Attributes - Help
:P.How a journal is set up: the receiver it writes to now, who hears
about it and how receivers are managed. F15 lists its receivers, F14
the objects it journals.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRNRD.Work with Receiver Directory - Help
:P.Every receiver chained to the journal, oldest first, with the time
it was attached. Option 8 shows a receiver's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPJRNOBJ.Display Journaled Objects - Help
:P.The objects whose changes the journal records, with the images it
keeps and the entries it leaves out.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/JAKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F14=Display journaled objects
:PD.Display journaled objects.
:PT.F15=Work with receiver directory
:PD.Work with receiver directory.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRN'.Journal
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ATTRCV'.Attached receiver
:P.The attached receiver shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRNTEXT'.Text
:P.The text shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASP'.ASP
:P.The ASP shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQ'.Message queue
:P.The message queue shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJCOUNT'.Journaled objects
:P.The journaled objects shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRNLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ATTRCVLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRNSTATE'.Journal state
:P.The journal state shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MNGRCV'.Manage receivers
:P.The manage receivers shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DLTRCV'.Delete receivers
:P.The delete receivers shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SUBKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNRD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RCV'.Receiver
:P.The receiver of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RCVLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RCVSTS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RCVATT'.Attached
:P.The attached of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNRD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Journal Receiver (DLTJRNRCV) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.8=Display attributes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to display attributes it.
The Display Journal Receiver Attr (DSPJRNRCVA) command runs for the
entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJ'.Object
:P.The object of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IMAGES'.Images
:P.The images of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OMTJRNE'.Omit
:P.The omit of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
